  "label": "Hateful",
  "description": "The meme directly attacks the concept of systemic racism by dismissing blame against the entire white race as inherently racist, using a false equivalence to justify racial blame-shifting. This is a hateful message because it targets an entire racial group based on historical actions of a minority within that group, using a false equivalence to justify racial blame-shifting. The visual of the finger pointing up is often used to signify 'I'm right' or 'you're wrong', reinforcing the confrontational and accusatory tone. The meme attempts to delegitimize racial discourse by conflating individual historical behavior with collective racial identity, which is a form of racialized hate speech that ignores the structural and systemic nature of racism.",
